 ࠎႿധ؇പࣜຩ઎ٳ֥ ሰ׮৯࿐൝ି૫࿐༝
[ABSTRACT]
Since its inception, the deep potential energy surface method has broken the dilemma
that molecular dynamics simulations cannot accurately calculate the long-term of multiple
atoms, making efficient calculation possible. At present, the molecular dynamics of deep
potential energy can be simulated for hundreds of millions of atoms, and has applications
in various fields of physics, chemistry, biology and medicine. Continuous research is also
ongoing, with different degrees of breakthroughs in the field of training data generation
and application. According to the principle of the molecular dynamics model of deep
potential energy, this paper obtains a descriptor that can preserve all natural symmetries
in the real system through the transformation of coordinates, the processing of weighted
functions, and the training of coding neural networks. This allows the potential energy of
the system to be trained in the deep neural network, independent of the system transla
tion, rotation and permutation transformation.This paper builds the basic code to achieve
the above functions, trains with two feed-forward neural networks, and obtains a fitted
potential energy that is close to the potential energy of the real system.
Keywords: deep potential energy, molecular dynamics, deep neural networks,invariant
